course: dictionary
lesson: 8463
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word sale is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which is its context. «A "For Sale" board means the family has decided to sell the house.» Here sale is about selling: the house is for sale, so someone wants to sell it.
explain: Now read this: «Mia wanted a new game, saw it would probably go on sale, and waited three whole impatient months.» Go on sale means it can be bought. Ask yourself what word would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
explain: Some meanings are about buying and selling in a bigger way. «The regulators, official checkers, test a medicine before doctors can prescribe it, and side effects are watched for after it goes on sale.» Here sale means the medicine is available for people to buy and use. The clue is that rare side effects only show up when many people use it.
fact: A sale is the act of selling something, such as the sale of a house.
fact: A sale is also a time when things cost less than usual, such as a summer sale.
fact: «For sale» means someone wants to sell it.
fact: «On sale» means it can be bought, or in the USA, that it is cheaper than usual.
fact: Sales can mean the number of things sold, or the money from them. A bake sale or yard sale is an event where people sell things.
exercise: «A "For Sale" board means the family has decided to sell the house.» What does «for sale» mean? | *Someone wants to sell it | The family is going on holiday | The house is empty and falling down | The house is very old
exercise: A summer sale is a time when things cost less than usual. What does sale mean here? | A shop that closes for the summer | A hot day at the beach | A party where people sing | *A time when things cost less than usual
exercise: A shop counts its sales for the month: 40 toys were sold. What does sales mean here? | *The number of things sold | A sad feeling about selling | A bake sale in the park | The price of the shop
test: «Mia wanted a new game, saw it would probably go on sale.» What does «on sale» mean? | *It can be bought | It has been lost | It is closed for repairs | It is painted red
test: What is a bake sale? | A cake with no sugar | A race for bakers | A shop that only sells bread | *An event where people sell cakes and other things
exam: In «the sale of a house», what does sale mean? | *The act of selling | Lower prices | A tasty dinner | A time when shops close
